# These files are compiled into the binary verbatim with `include_str!`.
# Normalize their bytes across platforms so a Windows package advertises the
# same resources, ships the same legal text, and parses the same data as the
# macOS and Linux packages built from the same commit.
#
# Without this, Git converts them to CRLF on a Windows checkout and every one
# of them is embedded with different bytes there. The rule used to name only
# `docs/skills/**/SKILL.md`, which left the rest of the set converted; a test
# asserting on a line break inside `docs/mcp-security-model.md` is what found
# the gap. Anything new reached by `include_str!` belongs in this list.
docs/mcp-server-instructions.md text eol=lf
docs/mcp-security-model.md text eol=lf
docs/policy-authoring.md text eol=lf
docs/skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md text eol=lf
contrib/polkit/com.ekubo.wallet.policy text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/networks.json text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/default-tokens.json text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/token-prices.json text eol=lf
crates/mcp-bridge/src/offline_capabilities.json text eol=lf
